    "media:imagetext": "FLOYD\nMI.\nF.E. Nelson,\nc/o China Nat'1\nAviation Corp.,\nChungking, China.\nDear Nellie,\n3 September, 1935.\nYour letter of August 10th arrived while I\nwas on a visit to the family at Peking following my return\nWhen I got back to Shanghai I learned that you\nwere in the city and tried all one afternoon to get in touch\nwith you, leaving word with your boy for you to call me at\nthe Metropole Hotel.\nI was very sorry I did not have a chance\nto see you at this time.\nYour letter about the trip to li Kiang is\nmost intriguing and I would like nothing better than the opp-\nortunity to join you on that expedition, however, it 1s nec-\nessary for me to return to Manila, leaving here on the 10th\nI will be away for over a month and during that\ntime you will undoubtedly return to Shanghai and I therefore\nsuggest that you report the opportunity for charter to the\nOperations Department for such consideration as they may wish\nto give Dr. Rock's proposition.\nI made a quick trip to Peiping last week and\nFrances, Bo and Ruth Stevens\nwere all away on a jaunt to the Diamond Mountains of Korea but\nwere due back on September Ist. Ruth is sailing on the Pres-\nident Hoover on September 10th and I am taking Frances\nwith me\nto Manila, sailing on the same date.\nAt the present time, the remaining members\nof the family have no definite plans.\nI hope you are having\ngood luck showing 0 Hara all the nice level Kansas-like fields\nin Kweichow and Yunnan and that you will soon be back in Shanghai.\nMrs. O Hara and Bud.\nPLease give my very kindest regards to 0 Hara,\nVery sincerely yours,\nH.M. Bixby\n3280,/S/.Plas",
